.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a 16‑bit IEEE‑754 binary16 floating‑point value with full bit‑level control over sign, exponent, and mantissa\&. 

\fBHalf16\fP is a deterministic, platform‑independent implementation of the half‑precision format\&. Unlike System\&.Half, this type exposes all internal fields, supports manual construction, and implements full arithmetic without converting to float\&.

.PP
The struct is sequentially laid out and marked with \fBHashAlgorithmAttribute\fP so that hashing can be performed deterministically using \fBSystemEx\fP hashing algorithms\&. 

.PP
\fBHalf16\fP also implements \fBIHashable<Half16>\fP so that instances can be converted into a deterministic byte sequence for hashing or serialization\&. 
.PP
